 "note": "Antwerp c.1650: the Spanish enceinte (1542-c.1567, the 'Spaanse omwalling'), the Scheldt front and the pentagonal citadel (1567-71), traced from the Ferraris map (1777), which shows them unchanged. Local metres around the Grote Markt (x east, z south). The ring follows the inner (curtain) line of the rampart on the land side; the projecting bastions and ravelins are not traced individually. The ring includes the citadel and the esplanade; the citadel's own enceinte is in forts[] (approximate, +-30 m). 'water' is the strip of the 17th-c. Scheldt between the old riverbank and today's quays (built 1877-85 on land reclaimed from the river).",
